From: Khanh Truong <khanhtd36@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 12:51:16 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] vendor(libghostty-vt): add prompt-aware terminal
 clear_screen and cursor_home C API

Export two FFI functions for herdr's clear_screen pane action:

- ghostty_terminal_clear_screen(): erases the primary screen's
  scrollback history always, and its active content according to
  whether the cursor is at an idle shell prompt (OSC 133
  semantic-prompt state, via the existing upstream
  Terminal.cursorIsAtPrompt() -- already used internally by real
  Ghostty's own clear_screen keybind action). If at a prompt, the
  entire active screen is cleared. Otherwise -- mid-command output, or
  no shell integration -- only rows strictly above the cursor's row are
  erased in place (VT100 ED1 semantics via Screen.clearRows; the
  cursor does not move), so the screen is never left blank with a
  stranded cursor when there is no shell integration to redraw a
  prompt afterward. It always targets the primary screen directly (not
  whichever screen is active), so it is safe to call while the
  alternate screen (vim, tmux) is active. Returns whether the cursor
  was at an idle prompt, so callers can decide whether to also home
  the cursor and nudge the shell to redraw its prompt, using the same
  prompt determination this function itself used.

  The not-at-prompt branch deliberately uses Screen.clearRows rather
  than Screen.eraseActive (which real Ghostty's own Termio.clearScreen
  uses for the same fallback): eraseActive physically removes and
  shifts pages, and does not reliably erase the full requested range
  when the active area spans more than one internal page -- e.g. a
  still-growing buffer (such as a fresh SSH session's login banner)
  that has not yet triggered real scrollback. clearRows clears cells
  in place via the same page-iteration that already works correctly
  for the at-prompt full-screen branch.
- ghostty_terminal_cursor_home(): moves the primary screen's cursor to
  (0, 0), always targeting the primary screen regardless of which
  screen is active, matching ghostty_terminal_clear_screen()'s
  primary-screen targeting.

Vendored base: c5a21edfcbc2d5b46540ad91b7980aca31f5f1f3
